4. Underlying data from Mountain High (reservation).
   a) Origin. The consumption figures on which the calculation is based do not
      originate from the rights holder. They are taken from the "Cylinder
      Duration Chart" (revision 06/2017) published by Mountain High Equipment
      & Supply Company, Redmond, Oregon, USA (www.mhoxygen.com): cylinder
      duration by cylinder size and altitude for one person, "EDS" columns.
   b) Rights. All rights in that chart and in the information it contains
      remain with Mountain High. This licence does not cover them; the rights
      holder claims no rights in them and cannot grant any. Consent under
      clause 2 does not extend to Mountain High's data; anyone wishing to use
      them must contact the manufacturer.
   c) Own contribution. The rights holder's own work comprises the conversion
      of the chart into consumption rates, the interpolation between
      altitudes, the assumptions outside the chart (below 10,000 ft, above
      25,000 ft, climb and descent), the calculation of cylinder content, and
      the program, design and texts. These derivations have been neither
      reviewed nor approved by the manufacturer.
   d) No warranty for the data. The rights holder does not warrant that the
      figures taken over are correct, complete or current. The manufacturer
      may change its specifications at any time; its documentation as
      currently in force prevails.
   e) No affiliation. "Mountain High", "EDS" and "O2D2" are designations or
      trademarks of the manufacturer. There is no business relationship with
      Mountain High; the work is neither commissioned nor supported or
      endorsed by the manufacturer.

